    "turn_text": "It is. Well, truth is truth, you know, but yeah, I think you're a great success, having raised your grandchildren right clearly, but so that's enough. I'd say your work is done, but we're glad it's not. We're glad you continued and I'm just going to ask you about some of the specifics in the book. Again, very timely, extremely prescient, the liberal majority in Congress passed a DC statehood bill and you address that very issue and the founding fathers wisdom in keeping Washington DC a very distinct entity, not that line within any state and not being a state in and of itself. Can you tell us a little bit about why that's so important?",
