    "turn_text": "That's just fascinating. And again, a really beautiful illustration. I also loved the story that you told about which, you know, we all should know this from our American history, but about George Washington surrendering his military commissioner, resigning his military commission in order to be a civil later. And the fact that that was something he was beloved. He was really giving up a lot of glory. He probably could have had a lot more power himself, but he was so committed to those ideals of limited government and being submissive to the people that he did resign his commission. Can you talk a little bit about that?",
