    "turn_text": "just feel so strongly about the rule of law because of my background. And when we look at American history, Again, we see people who have acted in a flawed way. You know, I talk about the fact that FDR used the IRS to punish his political opponents. And President Lyndon Mains Johnson used the CIA to spy on Barry Goldwater. And President Kennedy had one of his mistresses who was an East German spy, summarily deported, because of her activity and how embarrassing it would be. And President Obama used the IRS to deny conservative Tea Party groups the ability to form a nonprofit organization. So we have this long history of what happens when government grows too large and can be used by the left to punish political opponents. And it's one of the reasons why I think the rule of law is so important that even the FBI and how the Obama administration used the FBI to spy on the Trump campaign to prosecute individuals in the Trump campaign is fundamentally wrong. We need to abide by the rule of law and we need to understand that we are limited by the laws and how we deal with people and how we really form our government.",
